<article class="env-definition" id="00ZI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00ZI">Definition <span data-tag="00ZI">7.49.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Let $J$ be a topology on $\mathcal{C}$. We say that a presheaf of sets $\mathcal{F}$ is <em>separated</em> if for every object $U$ and every covering sieve $S$ on $U$ the canonical map $\mathcal{F}(U) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\textit{PSh}(\mathcal{C})}(S, \mathcal{F})$ is injective. </p>
</article>